pe":31}],"natures":["Timid"]},{"name":"Eviolite","pokemon":"Gastly","shiny":false,"gender":"DC","levels":[5],"description":"<p>These sample sets were uploaded on March 19, 2023, and are up-to-date for the current BW LC metagame.</p>","abilities":["Levitate"],"items":["Eviolite"],"teratypes":[],"moveslots":[[{"move":"Substitute","type":null}],[{"move":"Will-O-Wisp","type":null}],[{"move":"Sludge Bomb","type":null},{"move":"Pain Split","type":null}],[{"move":"Shadow Ball","type":null},{"move":"Pain Split","type":null}]],"evconfigs":[{"hp":116,"atk":0,"def":36,"spa":116,"spd":0,"spe":196}],"ivconfigs":[{"hp":31,"atk":0,"def":31,"spa":31,"spd":31,"spe":31}],"natures":["Timid"]}],"credits":{"writtenBy":[],"teams":[]}},{"format":"ZU","outdated":null,"overview":"","comments":"","movesets":[{"name":"Choice Scarf","pokemon":"Gastly","shiny":false,"gender":"DC","levels":[],"description":"<p>Gastly carves a niche for itself as a revenge killer thanks to its solid Special Attack and immunities to Normal, Fighting, and Ground; these immunities, particularly the immunity to <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/persian/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Persian</a>'s Fake Out, distinguish Gastly from more common Choice Scarf users like <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/simisear/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Simisear</a>, <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/mr-mime/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mr. Mime</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/grumpig/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Grumpig</a>. STAB Shadow Ball has great neutral coverage and hits staple offensive Pokemon like Grumpig, Mr. Mime, and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/solrock/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Solrock</a> very hard. Sludge Bomb grants a slightly stronger STAB move with decent neutral coverage against Normal-types and the occasional <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/vullaby/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Vullaby</a> while offering a very valuable super effective hit on the Grass-types, <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/meganium/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Meganium</a> and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/leafeon/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Leafeon</a>. Hidden Power Ground is critical coverage for Gastly to revenge kill Rock Polish <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/lairon/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Lairon</a>, but it has few other uses than catching Lairon and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/pawniard/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Pawniard</a> trying to switch in. Trick is Gastly's best method of disrupting walls like <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/clefairy/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Clefairy</a>, <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/wormadam-trash/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Wormadam-S</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/munchlax/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Munchlax</a>, and it allows Gastly to freely switch moves against slower teams.</p>\n<p>Choice Scarf Gastly is a good fit for offensive teams in need of a strong form of speed control that compresses several immunities. <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/muk/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Muk</a> is a huge issue for Gastly between its high special bulk and Shadow Sneak OHKOing Gastly, so Solrock is a great partner for Gastly. <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/arbok/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Arbok</a> makes a great partner to Gastly by checking Muk, and in turn, Gastly is often untouchable for passive walls like <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/hippopotas/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hippopotas</a> and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/vibrava/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Vibrava</a> that would trouble Arbok. <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/walrein/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Walrein</a> and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/whiscash/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Whiscash</a> can use Clefairy and Wormadam-S as setup fodder, so they appreciate Gastly luring them in while benefitting from the strong speed control Gastly offers, particularly against Leafeon. Partners like Muk and <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/mienfoo/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mienfoo</a> can cover Gastly's rough matchup against Clefairy while also absorbing special and physical hits, respectively. <a href=\"/dex/bw/pokemon/raichu/zu/\" hreflang=\"en\">Raichu</a> is a solid partner for Gastly that is capable of breaking Clefairy while benefitting from from Gastly threatening Meganium, which is often difficult for Raichu to break on its own, and faster attackers like Persian and Choice Scarf Mienfoo.</p>","abilities":["Levitate"],"items":["Choice Scarf"],"teratypes":[],"moveslots":[[{"move":"Shadow Ball","type":null}],[{"move":"Sludge Bomb","type":null}],[{"move":"Hidden Power","type":"Ground"}],[{"move":"Trick","type":null}]],"evconfigs":[{"hp":0,"atk":0,"def":0,"spa":252,"spd":4,"spe":252}],"ivconfigs":[{"hp":31,"atk":0,"def":31,"spa":31,"spd":31,"spe":31}],"natures":["Timid"]},{"name":"Stallbreaker","pokemon":"Gastly","shiny":false,"gender":"DC","levels":[],"description":"","abilities":["Levitate"],"items":["Black Sludge"],"teratypes":[],"moveslots":[[{"move":"Substitute","type":null}],[{"move":"Taunt","type":null}],[{"move":"Shadow Ball","type":null}],[{"move":"Sludge Bomb","type":null}]],"evconfigs":[{"hp":0,"atk":0,"def":0,"spa":252,"spd":4,"spe":252}],"ivconfigs":[{"hp":31,"atk":0,"def":31,"spa":31,"spd":31,"spe":31}],"natures":["Timid"]},{"name":"SubSplit","pokemon":"Gastly","shiny":false,"gender":"DC","levels":[],"description":"<p>Sample sets while we work on analyses.</p>","abilities":["Levitate"],"items":["Life Orb"],"teratypes":[],"moveslots":[[{"move":"Substitute","type":null}],[{"move":"Pain Split","type":null}],[{"move":"Shadow Ball","type":null}],[{"move":"Sludge Bomb","type":null}]],"evconfigs":[{"hp":0,"atk":0,"def":0,"spa":252,"spd":4,"spe":252}],"ivconfigs":[{"hp":31,"atk":0,"def":31,"spa":31,"spd":31,"spe":31}],"natures":["Timid"]}],"credits":{"writtenBy":[{"user_id":452572,"username":"missangelic"}],"teams":[{"name":"Quality checked by","members":[{"user_id":482455,"username":"Monai"},{"user_id":535530,"username":"Gangsta Spongebob"}]},{"name":"Grammar checked by","members":[{"user_id":555379,"username":"Tbolt"}]}]}}],"formeStrategies":[]}